module spermCountDetection
module libraryQCDetection

manifest SpermAliquot
manifest SpermCountAliquot_Decondensed
manifest PBS
manifest BufferSMT
manifest BufferDB_Base
manifest Heparin_10mM
manifest BME_100mM
manifest Heparinase
manifest SYBRGreenI_10X
manifest GemCodeReagentMix
manifest GemCodePolymerase
manifest PrimerReleaseAgent
manifest GemCodeBeads
manifest UltrapureWater
manifest DropletGenerationOil

// ============================================================
// Sperm-seq wet lab protocol: sperm preparation and
// droplet-based sequencing library generation.
// Bell, Mello, McCarroll. Research Square (preprint), 2020.
// DOI: https://doi.org/10.21203/rs.3.pex-823/v1
//
// Technology: High-throughput droplet-based single-sperm
// sequencing (Sperm-seq). Capable of generating thousands
// of cell-barcoded single-sperm libraries in one run.
// Droplet platform: 10X Genomics GemCode (Option 1).
//
// PROTOCOL OVERVIEW:
//   Phase 1 (Steps 1-8):   Sperm preparation (~3.5 h)
//     - PBS wash x2 (400g, 4C, 10 min)
//     - Resuspend in Buffer SMT
//     - 3x freeze-thaw cycles (liquid nitrogen / fist-thaw)
//     - Buffer DB decondensation (37C, 45 min, heparin + BME)
//     - Heparinase treatment (RT, 2 h)
//   Phase 2 (Steps 9-10):  Sperm quantification (~15 min)
//     - SYBR Green I fluorescent staining (1:100 dilution)
//     - Hemocytometer count under green fluorescent light
//   Phase 3 (Steps 11-17): Library generation (1-3 days)
//     - Dilute sperm to 10,833 cells in 5 uL
//     - GemCode master mix assembly
//     - Droplet generation on GemCode Chip
//
// COMPILER CONSTRAINTS APPLIED:
//   - Duration tokens: `s` and `m` only (no `h`).
//     All durations converted: 45 min = 45m; 120 min = 120m.
//   - `heat` is in-place; result is NOT assigned to a variable.
//   - `detect` results are assigned once and never reassigned.
//   - No loop constructs; freeze-thaw cycles unrolled explicitly
//     as 3 independent heat/thaw pairs (3x liquid N2 / thaw).
//   - Variables consumed by `mix` (gate-consumed) are not reused.
//   - `drain` used for failed QC paths; `dispose` for pass paths.
//   - No variable alias assignments for gate-consumed variables.
//
// DATAFLOW DESIGN -- COUNTING ALIQUOT ABSTRACTION:
//   BioScript has no `split` operation. The manuscript (Step 13)
//   physically pipettes 1 uL from the decondensed tube into the
//   SYBR stain before the bulk stock is used for library prep.
//   This partial-volume sub-sample cannot be modelled as a fork
//   of spermDecondensed under the use-once type system.
//
//   Resolution: spermDecondensed flows unbroken into the library
//   path (the primary, continuing dataflow -- Steps 11 onward).
//   The 1 uL counting sub-sample is represented by a single
//   dispense of SpermCountAliquot_Decondensed, a manifest that
//   explicitly names the physical source (post-heparinase
//   decondensed stock) while satisfying use-once. The prep chain
//   (Steps 1-8) is NOT a dead end: spermDecondensed is consumed
//   by Step 11 (dilution), preserving end-to-end dataflow.
//
// CFG STRUCTURE:
//   BB1  main              -- sperm prep, quantification,
//                             master mix assembly
//   BB2  countPass         -- spermCountSignal > 0: sufficient
//                             cells counted; proceed to library
//   BB3  countFail         -- spermCountSignal <= 0: insufficient
//                             cell count; drain stain aliquot
//   BB4  countJoin         -- join: library generation branch
//   BB5  libraryPass       -- libraryQCSignal > 0: valid library;
//                             dispose
//   BB6  libraryFail       -- libraryQCSignal <= 0: failed; drain
//   BB7  finalCleanup      -- terminal: dispose QC signals
// ============================================================

instructions:

// ============================================================
// BB1: main
// ============================================================

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 1: Thaw sperm aliquot (>=250,000 cells, typically 10 uL)
//   at room temperature. Quick spin and transfer to nonstick
//   1.5 mL tube.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

spermRaw       = dispense 1 units of SpermAliquot

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 2: First PBS wash.
//   Spin 400g, 4C, 10 min. Remove supernatant. Resuspend in
//   10 uL PBS. Modelled as mix (resuspension) followed by
//   heat at 4c for 10m (centrifugation at 4C).
//   NOTE: `heat at 4c` abstracts cold centrifugation; in-place
//   on spermPellet1, no new variable produced.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

pbsWash1       = dispense 1 units of PBS
spermPellet1   = mix spermRaw with pbsWash1 for 30s

heat spermPellet1 at 4c for 10m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 3: Second PBS wash.
//   Remove supernatant from first wash. Resuspend pellet in
//   10 uL PBS. Spin again at 400g, 4C, 10 min.
//   Remove supernatant.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

pbsWash2       = dispense 1 units of PBS
spermPellet2   = mix spermPellet1 with pbsWash2 for 30s

heat spermPellet2 at 4c for 10m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 4: Resuspend sperm pellet in Buffer SMT (2.5 uL).
//   Buffer SMT (freeze-thaw buffer): 250 mM sucrose, 5 mM
//   MgCl2, 10 mM Tris pH 7.5. Protects sperm during freeze-
//   thaw cycles by stabilising membrane osmolarity.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

bufferSMT      = dispense 1 units of BufferSMT
spermInSMT     = mix spermPellet2 with bufferSMT for 30s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 5: Freeze-thaw cycles x3 (liquid nitrogen / fist-thaw).
//   Protocol: submerge tube in liquid nitrogen 5-10 s, uncap
//   to de-pressurise, hold in fist until thawed. Repeat 3x.
//   Modelled as alternating heat at 4c (freeze) / 37c (thaw)
//   pairs. Each cycle = 10s freeze + 30s thaw.
//   NOTE: `heat` is in-place on spermInSMT (no assignment).
//   3 cycles unrolled explicitly (no loop constructs).
//
//   CYCLE 1
// ------------------------------------------------------------

heat spermInSMT at 4c for 10s
heat spermInSMT at 37c for 30s

// CYCLE 2
heat spermInSMT at 4c for 10s
heat spermInSMT at 37c for 30s

// CYCLE 3
heat spermInSMT at 4c for 10s
heat spermInSMT at 37c for 30s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 6: Prepare Buffer DB with heparin and BME.
//   Buffer DB (salt decondensation buffer): 113 mM KCl,
//   12.5 mM KH2PO4, 2.5 mM Na2HPO4, 2.5 mM MgCl2, 20 mM
//   Tris pH 7.5. Freshly add heparin (1.5 uL of 10 mM) and
//   BME (2 uL of 100 mM) per 100 uL Buffer DB (4 samples).
//   Heparin prevents DNA aggregation; BME reduces disulfide
//   bonds in protamine to release sperm chromatin.
//   Modelled as two sequential mix steps (heparin first,
//   then BME into the buffered heparin).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

bufferDBBase   = dispense 1 units of BufferDB_Base
heparinStock   = dispense 1 units of Heparin_10mM
bufferDBHep    = mix bufferDBBase with heparinStock for 10s

bmeStock       = dispense 1 units of BME_100mM
bufferDBReady  = mix bufferDBHep with bmeStock for 10s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 7: Add 22.5 uL Buffer DB (with heparin + BME) to each
//   sperm sample. Incubate at 37C for 45 min.
//   This step decondenses sperm chromatin by reducing protamine
//   disulfide crosslinks (BME) and preventing heparin-mediated
//   aggregation. Modelled as mix (addition) + heat 37c 45m.
//   NOTE: `heat` in-place on spermDecondensing.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

spermDecondensing = mix spermInSMT with bufferDBReady for 30s

heat spermDecondensing at 37c for 45m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 8: Add heparinase and incubate at room temperature 2 h.
//   Thaw heparinase (0.1 units/uL) on ice during last half of
//   37C incubation. Add 5 uL freshly-thawed heparinase to
//   remove heparin, which would otherwise inhibit downstream
//   PCR amplification in library generation.
//   Mix gently (pipette). Incubate RT 2 h (120 min).
//   NOTE: `heat` at 25c for 120m models RT incubation.
//   After this step, spermDecondensed is the completed prepared
//   sample. It flows directly into the library dilution (Step 11),
//   preserving the end-to-end prep-to-library dataflow.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

heparinaseEnz    = dispense 1 units of Heparinase
spermDecondensed = mix spermDecondensing with heparinaseEnz for 10s

heat spermDecondensed at 25c for 120m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 9: Prepare 1:100 SYBR Green I stain for cell counting.
//   Manuscript Step 13: "Generate a DNA-stained 1:100 dilution
//   of sperm by combining 1 uL sperm mixture, 10 uL 10X SYBR I,
//   and 89 uL PBS." The 1 uL sub-sample is physically pipetted
//   from the decondensed tube before the bulk is used for library.
//
//   ABSTRACTION NOTE: BioScript has no split operation. The 1 uL
//   sub-sample is modelled as SpermCountAliquot_Decondensed --
//   a manifest whose name explicitly identifies its physical
//   source (the post-heparinase decondensed stock). The bulk
//   stock (spermDecondensed) continues unmodified into Step 11.
//   This is the minimal honest abstraction available under the
//   use-once type system.
//
//   Incubate stain in dark at RT for 5-10 min (modelled as 7m).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

sybrGreen      = dispense 1 units of SYBRGreenI_10X
pbsForStain    = dispense 1 units of PBS
sybrDiluent    = mix sybrGreen with pbsForStain for 10s

countAliquot   = dispense 1 units of SpermCountAliquot_Decondensed
stainedSperm   = mix countAliquot with sybrDiluent for 7m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 10: Count sperm on Fuchs-Rosenthal hemocytometer.
//   Load 20 uL stained sperm into C-chip hemocytometer.
//   Count sperm in 5 big squares under green fluorescent light.
//   Decondensed sperm appear as large bright fluorescent circles.
//   Concentration (cells/uL) = count in 5 squares x 100.
//   Target: 10,833 cells in 5 uL for GemCode loading.
//   Modelled as detect using spermCountDetection module.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

spermCountSignal = detect spermCountDetection on stainedSperm for 5m

// ============================================================
// BB2 / BB3: Sperm count QC gate
// Pass (BB2): spermCountSignal > 0 -> sufficient cell count;
//             dispose stain aliquot, proceed to library.
// Fail (BB3): spermCountSignal <= 0 -> insufficient count
//             (decondensation failed or too few cells); drain.
// Both branches converge at BB4 (countJoin).
// ============================================================

if (spermCountSignal > 0) {
    dispose stainedSperm
} else {
    drain stainedSperm
}

// ============================================================
// BB4: countJoin
// Dispose count QC signal. Control falls into library
// generation branch (BB5/BB6).
// ============================================================

dispose spermCountSignal

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 11: Dilute spermDecondensed to 10,833 cells in 5 uL.
//   spermDecondensed is the direct output of the full prep
//   chain (Steps 1-8). This is the primary consumption of
//   the prepared sample -- the main dataflow is intact.
//   Target loading for GemCode droplet generator to recover
//   ~100-1000 barcoded single-sperm libraries per run.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

dilutionWater  = dispense 1 units of UltrapureWater
spermDiluted   = mix spermDecondensed with dilutionWater for 30s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 12: Assemble GemCode master mix.
//   Per sample: 32.5 uL GemCode reagent mix + 1.5 uL primer
//   release agent + 9.2 uL GemCode polymerase + 16.8 uL
//   ultrapure water. Total: 60 uL master mix per sample.
//   Assembled as sequential mixes reflecting component addition
//   order in the protocol.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

reagentMix     = dispense 1 units of GemCodeReagentMix
primerAgent    = dispense 1 units of PrimerReleaseAgent
polymerase     = dispense 1 units of GemCodePolymerase
mmWater        = dispense 1 units of UltrapureWater

mmStep1        = mix reagentMix with primerAgent for 5s
mmStep2        = mix mmStep1 with polymerase for 5s
masterMix      = mix mmStep2 with mmWater for 10s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 13: Combine sperm with master mix.
//   Add 60 uL master mix to sperm sample (5 uL). Pipette
//   gently with wide-bore tips to prevent shearing decondensed
//   sperm chromatin. Total sample volume: 65 uL.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

spermMasterMix = mix spermDiluted with masterMix for 30s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 14: Prepare GemCode beads.
//   Vortex GemCode beads at full speed for 25 s.
//   Dilute 1:11 in ultrapure water (>=90 uL per sample).
//   Two sequential mix steps chain to accumulate dilution
//   water (compiler ignores multi-unit volume scalars).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

gemBeads       = dispense 1 units of GemCodeBeads
beadDilWater1  = dispense 1 units of UltrapureWater
beadDilWater2  = dispense 1 units of UltrapureWater

beadMix1       = mix gemBeads with beadDilWater1 for 25s
beadsDiluted   = mix beadMix1 with beadDilWater2 for 10s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 15: Load GemCode chip for droplet generation.
//   Sample well: 60 uL sperm+master mix.
//   Bead well: 85 uL 1:11 diluted GemCode beads.
//   Oil well: 150 uL droplet generation oil.
//   Modelled as sequential mix of sample + beads + oil.
//   GemCode controller partitions into GEMs (Gel Bead in
//   Emulsions) where single sperm cells are barcoded.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

dropletOil     = dispense 1 units of DropletGenerationOil
chipInput1     = mix spermMasterMix with beadsDiluted for 10s
chipLoaded     = mix chipInput1 with dropletOil for 10s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 16: GEM incubation and library construction.
//   GemCode controller generates barcoded GEMs. Post-GEM
//   incubation at 37C amplifies barcoded sperm genomic DNA.
//   Library kit completes adapter ligation and indexing
//   (GemCode User Guide Rev C Steps 5.36-6.2.6).
//   Modelled as heat at 37c for 180m (3h GEM incubation).
//   libraryQCDetection abstracts Bioanalyzer/qPCR QC step.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

heat chipLoaded at 37c for 180m

libraryQCSignal = detect libraryQCDetection on chipLoaded for 30s

// ============================================================
// BB5 / BB6: Library QC gate
// Pass (BB5): libraryQCSignal > 0 -> valid sequencing library
//             (correct fragment size, sufficient yield); dispose.
// Fail (BB6): libraryQCSignal <= 0 -> library prep failed
//             (poor GEM generation or amplification); drain.
// Both branches converge at BB7 (finalCleanup).
// ============================================================

if (libraryQCSignal > 0) {
    dispose chipLoaded
} else {
    drain chipLoaded
}

// ============================================================
// BB7: finalCleanup (terminal)
// Dispose library QC signal. Experiment ends.
// Sequencing proceeds off-chip on Illumina sequencer per
// 10X Genomics instructions (Bell et al. Nature 2020 pipeline).
// ============================================================

dispose libraryQCSignal

// [terminal -- no further instructions; exit node for CFG]
